From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: krane <chris@krane.dev>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 01:10:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Translator: paste icon follows its own button

Problem: the paste icon greyed out whenever the input was empty.

Port: the icon uses a fixed colOnLayer1, since pasteButton is always
enabled. Upstream coloured it from deleteButton.enabled, which greyed
it out on an empty input.

Drop when: the pinned Translator.qml paste icon colour no longer
depends on deleteButton.enabled.
---
 .../.config/quickshell/ii/modules/ii/sidebarLeft/Translator.qml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dots/.config/quickshell/ii/modules/ii/sidebarLeft/Translator.qml b/dots/.config/quickshell/ii/modules/ii/sidebarLeft/Translator.qml
index 59de63cd..f018a8ba 100644
--- a/dots/.config/quickshell/ii/modules/ii/sidebarLeft/Translator.qml
+++ b/dots/.config/quickshell/ii/modules/ii/sidebarLeft/Translator.qml
@@ -190,7 +190,7 @@ Item {
                     horizontalAlignment: Text.AlignHCenter
                     iconSize: Appearance.font.pixelSize.larger
                     text: "content_paste"
-                    color: deleteButton.enabled ? Appearance.colors.colOnLayer1 : Appearance.colors.colSubtext
+                    color: Appearance.colors.colOnLayer1
                 }
                 onClicked: {
                     root.inputField.text = Quickshell.clipboardText
